.TH TIMERC-UNINSTALL 1 "2026" "timerc 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timerc-uninstall \- remove timerc from the system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timerc-uninstall
[\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-purge\fR]
.br
.B timerc uninstall
[\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-purge\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes everything the installer put under the install prefix: the
.BR timerc ,
.B timerc-bg
and
.B timerc-uninstall
commands, the man pages, the desktop entry and the icon, plus the setuid
.B timerc-lock-helper
if present. The prefix is derived from where the running binary lives (it must
be in a \fIbin/\fR directory), so it works for any \fBPREFIX\fR, including the
default \fI~/.local\fR. The files are listed first and removed only after you
confirm.
.PP
Your settings, history and log in \fI~/.config/timerc\fR are kept unless
.B \-\-purge
is given.
.PP
If timerc was installed from the \fB.deb\fR package, use
.B sudo apt remove timerc
instead; the command says so and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation (required when not run from a terminal).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Only list what would be removed.
.TP
.B \-\-purge
Also delete \fIconfig.conf\fR, \fIdata.db\fR and \fItimer.log\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if something could not be removed (the command then suggests
re-running with sudo) or the user aborted, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timerc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
